Here’s the recommended front-end functionality outline for LocalMind, optimized for Stitch design.

LocalMind Front-End Interface
1. Home / Dashboard

Purpose: simple entry point.

Should include:

App name: LocalMind
Tagline: AI That Stays With You
Button: Upload Documents
Button: Ask a Question
Recent documents list
Knowledge base status:
Number of uploaded documents
Number of indexed chunks
Last updated date
2. Document Upload Page

Core functionality:

Drag-and-drop upload area
File picker button
Supported file types:
PDF
DOCX
TXT
Upload progress indicator
Processing status:
Uploading
Extracting text
Chunking document
Creating embeddings
Stored in knowledge base
Confirmation message when complete

Optional:

Document category/tag field
Delete uploaded document button
3. Document Library

Purpose: show all stored knowledge sources.

Should include:

List or card view of uploaded documents
File name
File type
Upload date
Processing status
Number of text chunks
Actions:
View summary
Ask questions about this document
Delete document

This page helps demonstrate Document Ingestion & Knowledge Storage.

4. AI Q&A Page

This is the most important screen.

Core elements:

Large question input box
Button: Ask LocalMind
Option to search:
All documents
Selected document
AI answer area
Citation section under answer
Source references showing:
Document name
Page number or section
Relevant excerpt

Example citation display:

Source: AI_Ethics_Report.pdf, Page 4
“Responsible AI systems should prioritize transparency and accountability.”

This directly supports the 40-point grading category.

5. Semantic Search Page

Purpose: show that the system understands meaning, not just keywords.

Core elements:

Search bar
Search results ranked by relevance
Each result should show:
Document name
Relevance score
Short text snippet
Button: “Use in Q&A”
Button: “View source”

This helps demonstrate semantic retrieval.

6. Summary Page

Purpose: generate document summaries.

Core elements:

Select document dropdown
Button: Generate Summary
Summary output options:
Short summary
Detailed summary
Key points
Action items
Copy summary button

This supports the Summaries & Semantic Retrieval category.

7. Study / Quiz Mode

Keep this simple because it is only worth 10 points.

Core elements:

Select document
Button: Generate Quiz
Options:
Multiple choice
True/false
Short answer
Display generated questions
Show answer button
Score summary

Optional:

Generate flashcards
8. Settings Page

Keep minimal.

Should include:

Model selection:
Local model
Cloud model, if applicable
Knowledge base management:
Clear all documents
Rebuild index
Privacy message:
“Your documents stay local unless cloud processing is enabled.”
Recommended Navigation Menu

Use a clean sidebar or top navigation:

Dashboard
Upload
Library
Ask
Search
Summarize
Quiz Mode
Settings
Best Stitch Prompt

Use this prompt in Stitch:

Design a clean, modern web app interface for “LocalMind – AI That Stays With You,” a privacy-focused AI knowledge assistant. The app lets users upload documents, build a local knowledge base, ask questions with citations, perform semantic search, generate summaries, and create simple quizzes from uploaded documents.

Create screens for:
1. Dashboard
2. Document Upload
3. Document Library
4. AI Q&A with citations
5. Semantic Search
6. Document Summary
7. Study / Quiz Mode
8. Settings

Use a polished academic and professional style, suitable for a college AI capstone presentation. Include a calm color palette, sidebar navigation, document cards, chat-style Q&A area, citation cards, upload progress indicators, and clear privacy-focused messaging.

This front end should visually prove the project meets the professor’s grading categories.
